#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Summarize the frozen legacy/equation/navigation comparison."""
import json,statistics
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'reports/multiformat-legacy-quality-2026-11-12'
def read(p):return json.loads(p.read_text())
def main():
 s=read(OUT/'benchmark-final/summary.json');q=read(OUT/'quality-results.json');env=read(OUT/'benchmark-final/environment.json');c=read(OUT/'change-summary.json')
 lines=['# Legacy Office, equations and EPUB navigation — 12 November 2026','',
 'The ten previously failing source checks now pass using BulkParse-owned extraction rules. Changes cover Word/RTF paragraph formatting, ODF equations, legacy PowerPoint notes, EPUB metadata/internal navigation and ODS duration display. Additional work preserves equations in EPUB, PPTX and RTF. AnyDoc and Docling were reviewed as design references, and remain benchmark-only dependencies. No model, OCR, LibreOffice or remote converter is used by these readers.','',
 '## Quality comparison','',
 '| Source-grounded checks | BulkParse before | BulkParse after | AnyDoc |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
 for name,label in [('previous_45','Previous 45 checks'),('additional_equations','Additional equation checks')]:
  r=q['cohorts'][name];lines.append(f"| {label} | {r['before']}/{r['checks']} | {r['after']}/{r['checks']} | {r['anydoc']}/{r['checks']} |")
 lines += [f"| Total | {q['totals']['before']}/{q['checks']} | {q['totals']['after']}/{q['checks']} | {q['totals']['anydoc']}/{q['checks']} |",'',
 'No previously passing selected check regressed. The previous 45 retain their intended facts: the anchor check now verifies that a named link resolves to an emitted anchor, without requiring AnyDoc’s specific ID spelling; the RTF heading check permits emphasis within a valid heading. Applying these equivalent checks to the frozen previous outputs still gives 35/45 for BulkParse and 42/45 for AnyDoc. Nine additional checks cover source equation structures; they are not inferred from matching AnyDoc text.','',
 '**These are development checks, not a whole-document quality score or an independent holdout.** The three checks AnyDoc misses concern chartsheet content and spreadsheet comments from the previous work. A 54/54 result does not establish overall superiority or reproduce AnyDoc’s private 100-document LLM benchmark. Equation checks verify selected structures and content, not every possible mathematical expression or rendering engine.','',
 f"All **{c['returned']}/{c['conversion_documents']} conversion inputs** return output. **{c['changed_outputs']} Markdown outputs changed** versus the previous implementation. The detected status count changes from 65 partial / 16 complete to **62 partial / 19 complete**. Most partial flags concern features outside these targeted checks; completeness is not a measured fraction, and a complete status is not proof of perfect fidelity.",'',
 'The [check manifest](quality-checks.json) records source and package-part hashes, exact expectations, and cohorts. [Detailed results](quality-results.json) include every outcome. The [partial audit](partial-audit.md) covers the previous 65 partial inputs; [output-change review](output-change-review.json) covers all changed predictions, including changes to previously complete outputs.','',
 '## Same-machine benchmark','',
 f"Machine: **{env['machine']}**, {env['platform']}. BulkParse {env['versions']['bulkparse']} (schema **0.5**), AnyDoc {env['versions']['anydoc']}, Docling {env['versions']['docling']}. The frozen corpus remains 70 upstream conversion fixtures plus 11 authored inputs; nine malformed/resource-stress inputs run separately.",'',
 '| Engine | Returned / attempted | Median full-corpus time | Lifetime peak RSS |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
 for e,r in s['engines'].items():lines.append(f"| {e} | {r['returned']}/{r['attempted']} | {r['median_corpus_ms']:.3f} ms | {s['resources'][e]['lifetime_peak_rss_bytes']/1048576:.1f} MiB |")
 runs={e:[read(OUT/f'benchmark-final/{e}-pass-{i}.json')['documents'] for i in range(1,6)] for e in s['engines']};common=set.intersection(*[{r['path'] for r in v[0] if r['ok']} for v in runs.values()])
 times={e:statistics.median(sum(r['elapsed_ns'] for r in run if r['path'] in common)/1e6 for run in v) for e,v in runs.items()}
 lines += ['',
 'BulkParse and AnyDoc process the identical 81 inputs. Docling only attempts the 31 XLSX/XLSM/PPTX inputs supported by this comparison worker; its six previous synthetic PPTX failures remain in the timings. On the **same 25 inputs returned by all three**, medians are '+', '.join(f"{e} **{v:.3f} ms**" for e,v in times.items())+'.','',
 'Protocol: one excluded full warm-up, then five sequential full-corpus runs with rotating engine order. Persistent processes exclude startup from conversion clocks; file reads, parsing and default Markdown export are included. IPC, output serialization/writes and scoring are excluded. Corpus timing sums per-document clocks; thread settings are one and conversions do not overlap. Five-pass predictions and outcomes are deterministic. RSS is the macOS process-lifetime peak, including warm-up and, for Rust workers, the separate robustness pass. It is not incremental per-document memory. Lifetime CPU includes startup and is recorded in the raw resource logs.','',
 'BulkParse’s historical previous run took 18.113 ms with 13.7 MiB peak RSS. The current run takes 19.146 ms with 13.9 MiB while extracting more content. This is a comparison of separate runs, not interleaved old/new binaries. Current BulkParse conversion time is about 21% lower than AnyDoc’s. Different output scope still affects comparisons; these small development fixtures on macOS do not establish Linux production throughput.','',
 '### Per-format timings','',
 '| Format | Inputs | BulkParse median document ms | AnyDoc median document ms | BulkParse partial |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
 for fmt,eng in s['per_format'].items():
  b=eng['bulkparse'];a=eng['anydoc'];lines.append(f"| {fmt.upper()} | {b['attempted']} | {b['median_document_ms']:.3f} | {a['median_document_ms']:.3f} | {b['partial']} |")
 lines += ['',
 'Median document time first takes each input’s five-run median, then the median over inputs of that extension. Failed attempts remain in timing aggregates. XLSM is an alias, not another parser.','',
 '## Implementation and references','',
 '- **Legacy Word:** reads STSH style definitions, parent chains and FKP paragraph/character runs, mapping supported properties into emphasis and heading/code/quote blocks. Adjacent code and quote paragraphs coalesce. Piece-table text stays in the existing reader; malformed optional formatting falls back to text with a diagnostic. Full Word property language, lists, floating objects, footnotes/endnotes and table geometry remain incomplete.',
 '- **RTF:** a bounded prelude/equation pass reads inherited paragraph styles and structured math groups while respecting binary lengths and Unicode escapes. The existing reader still handles ordinary text and control state. Code whitespace, heading levels and explicit resets are preserved. Complex merged tables, full numbering and auxiliary stories remain incomplete.',
 '- **Equations:** a shared bounded MathML/OMML mapper generates TeX for fractions, roots, scripts, sums, functions, matrices and related supported structures. ODF package-local and inline objects work; replacement images are skipped when the equation is recovered. PPTX selects its equation-bearing compatibility branch once and preserves surrounding text. RTF display groups and EPUB MathML retain structure; annotation strings are not executed. Unknown structures retain available children and report a gap. This is not a full TeX engine or universal equation implementation.',
 '- **PowerPoint notes:** resolves active note containers through the persistence directory and matches `NotesAtom.slideIdRef` to slide IDs. Sparse notes do not attach to the wrong slide; unmatched active notes are retained at the end with a diagnostic. Damaged active persistence is still rejected instead of scanning obsolete slide records. Legacy rich layout/formatting remains incomplete.',
 '- **EPUB:** exports metadata titles, EPUB 3 navigation documents and body/inline ID targets. Package-relative, percent-encoded and cross-chapter links resolve to case-sensitive, collision-free generated anchors. Duplicate and missing/hidden targets are diagnosed. External links remain external and are not fetched. Full CSS, EPUB 2 NCX-only contents and image pixels remain incomplete.',
 '- **ODS durations:** renders bounded day/week/hour/minute/second durations, including negative and fractional elapsed values. Calendar-dependent or oversized values remain in their original literal form.',
 '- Production rules inspect format records, relationships, standard style names and expression trees. They contain no benchmark filenames, document identifiers, fixture strings or score-based branches. Source checks intentionally contain fixture expectations.','',
 'AnyDoc’s direct Word STSH/FKP decoding, RTF style inheritance, sparse slide-note matching, math traversal and block-style grouping informed the design. Docling’s Word/PPTX equation fragments and separate note handling reinforced keeping structured expressions distinct from plain text. Docling converts legacy DOC through LibreOffice; that path was not adopted. Its EPUB backend documents that Markdown anchor IDs are not preserved, so copying its fragment-only link rewrite would not solve this task. BulkParse validates links against actual exported targets. The exact local reference files and hashes are in [design-reference-hashes.json](design-reference-hashes.json); licenses remain in [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](../../THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).','',
 '## Schema and validation','',
 'The shared schema advances from **0.4 to 0.5**, adding `Inline::Math { tex, display }` and `Inline::Anchor { id }`. JSON preserves these semantics and Markdown renders them. Consumers enforcing 0.4 or exhaustively matching inline variants must update. PDF inspection uses the shared version string; its fields are unchanged.','',
 '- **197 all-feature Rust workspace tests pass**, including **37 Office tests** (11 new tests). Minimal core: **21**; Office-only core: **58**. Workspace Clippy with warnings denied and formatting checks pass.',
 '- The new tests vary style IDs/parent chains, explicit overrides, corrupt metadata, equation structures, sparse note ownership, anchor casing and targets. Bounds and unsafe equation-text handling are tested. These are authored regression tests, not an unseen corpus.',
 '- Node and Python each pass four smoke tests; WASM smoke tests pass. Standard parity: **19 conversions + three inspections** across Node/Python/WASM/CLI. Extended parity: **26 conversions + three inspections** using `node --liftoff-only`.',
 '- The previously recorded default Node 24.21.0 optimizing-compiler OOM on large PDF/WASM cases remains a known limitation; this task does not claim it is fixed or that default extended parity passed. Linux/browser validation remains outstanding.',
 '- **All 200 reference PDF Markdown predictions remain byte-for-byte unchanged** using the benchmarked binary. The inputs to NID/TEDS/MHS are unchanged; PDF timing and metric scoring were not rerun for these Office changes.',
 '- Existing authored semantic checks remain **11/11** for BulkParse and AnyDoc, and **2/2** for Docling’s supported authored inputs. Separate robustness outcomes are unchanged: BulkParse rejects eight and recovers one RTF; AnyDoc rejects seven and recovers that RTF plus a damaged-persistence PPT. No crashes occurred in this set.','',
 '## Reproduce and download','',
 'Restore the hash-matched upstream corpora and comparison environments using the [multiformat protocol](../../benchmarks/multiformat/README.md). All predicates and predictions are available; no quality score is invented.','',
 '```sh','cargo test --workspace --all-features','cargo build --release -p bulkparse --example office_bench','python3 scripts/benchmark_office_formats.py --out reports/my-legacy-run','python3 scripts/validate_office_benchmark.py reports/my-legacy-run','python3 scripts/evaluate_office_quality.py --run reports/my-legacy-run \\','  --baseline reports/multiformat-quality-2026-11-12/benchmark-final \\','  --spec reports/multiformat-legacy-quality-2026-11-12/quality-checks.json \\','  --out reports/my-legacy-evaluation','python3 scripts/check_office_pdf_regression.py --out reports/my-legacy-evaluation/pdf-regression.json','```','',
 '- [Download source and evidence ZIP](../multiformat-legacy-quality-2026-11-12.zip). Third-party input documents, dependencies, models and compiled binaries are excluded.',
 '- [Benchmark summary](benchmark-final/summary.json), [environment/binary hashes](benchmark-final/environment.json), [corpus manifest](benchmark-final/manifest.json), [source hashes](benchmark-final/source-manifest.json).',
 '- Raw warm-up/five-pass outcomes, complete predictions, resource logs and robustness outputs are in `benchmark-final`.',
 '- [Validation](validation/summary.json), [PDF equality](pdf-regression.json), [quality checks](quality-results.json), [previous report](../multiformat-quality-2026-11-12/README.md).','']
 (OUT/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
